# Host rules. Order matters: the first match wins, so the canonical-host
# redirects have to sit above the SPA fallback or the fallback swallows them.

# Canonical host is www. Confirmed with the client; the whole site — canonical
# tags, sitemap, robots.txt and JSON-LD — is built around it, so the apex has
# to redirect rather than serve a second copy of every page. Without this the
# same 49 URLs exist twice and the ranking signals split between them.
# 301 (not 302) so the move is treated as permanent, and `!` so the rule is
# applied even where a path would otherwise resolve.
http://prestigetutelage.co.za/*    https://www.prestigetutelage.co.za/:splat  301!
https://prestigetutelage.co.za/*   https://www.prestigetutelage.co.za/:splat  301!
http://www.prestigetutelage.co.za/*  https://www.prestigetutelage.co.za/:splat  301!

# Client-side routing: every unmatched path is served the app shell, which then
# renders the route. 200 rather than a redirect so the URL the visitor asked
# for is the URL that stays in the address bar.
/*  /index.html  200
